<urn:usf:requirement:fixture-runtime-native-metadata> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Run the existing fixture-process-confined test unchanged under both mode1 and mode2; its path-based chmod is allowed under current mode1 and was already actually proven. Do not confuse chmod(path) with the categorically disabled FileHandle.chmod/fchmod API. The native-only test must assert process.permission is absent, open a bounded scratch file, call FileHandle.chmod(0600) on the descriptor, close it, and observe exact mode, uid, inode type/link count and payload; prove rename inside scratch and exact old-path ENOENT. Create a relative symlink to a known scratch target; observe symlink inode, exact readlink value and target payload. Required positive API errors must fail, never skip or become proof. For known existing read-only execution-view source and tool paths, attempt descriptor/path metadata mutation and a new symlink destination; require only EACCES, EPERM or EROFS and exact unchanged contents/mode plus absent new path. Do not read or mutate ambient host files. A symlink in scratch aimed at a known read-only execution-view file must not permit an append/overwrite; require exact OS permission/read-only error and unchanged target bytes. Native outside-scratch writes require OS error EACCES/EPERM/EROFS, never Node ERR_ACCESS_DENIED, arbitrary failures or missing-path errors. Retain original environment/UID/PID/network route/exact tool/lock contention+bounded release/AF_UNIX named+abstract/INET/shell/interpreter/loader/scratch-copied native denials. Keep default Node ERR_ACCESS_DENIED check in its own default obligation. Independent construction/currentness/check/integration/completion for the broadened scope must all pass; native fixture evidence is not actual host stewardship or takeover." <urn:usf:graph:fixture-process-runtime> .
<urn:usf:requirement:fixture-runtime-native-metadata> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:fixture-process-runtime> .
