<urn:usf:requirement:fixture-runtime-peer-identity> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "USF-1185: require a fifth separate mode2 fixture-process-peer-identity test using current linuxProcessInspector from src/continuous/lifecycle.ts and its exact core/canonical.ts and core/errors.ts dependencies. Preserve every existing four obligation command and assertion. Reassert native mode, private process PID2/PPID1 and exact numeric one-row uid_map[1000,0,1]. Require actual inspector failure EACCES or EPERM for private namespace-init PID1; never use a host PID, remove executablePathDigest or replace identity with caller assertions. Obtain parent current identity, spawn only the admitted Node executable with fixed ESM child script and bounded standard streams; child obtains its own current identity and inspects its actual parent, reports one bounded JSON line, and remains alive until the parent explicitly releases stdin. Parent deep-compares child-reported parent with its own current identity, observes the live child with the same inspector and deep-compares every identity field including executablePathDigest and argvDigest. Require child.pid identity, same owner, bounded report <=16KiB, per-phase timeout<=5000ms, exact release and exit0, and kill/await only this owned fixture child on failure. No promise-only abandoned waiter, arbitrary error acceptance, skip or weakened identity. This proves same-confined-peer read/readby and exclusion of the namespace-init peer; it does not prove live-host stewardship, attach/trace, deployment or production. Keep full existing positive/negative mode1/default/mode2 metadata, network/socket/io_uring, readonly tools/source, native-exec/loader/scratch-copy and lock obligations. Exact profile source/kernel identities, scope, tools, checks, integration and completion must be current." <urn:usf:graph:fixture-process-runtime> .
